Subject: [PATCH] winex11: Show the current frame of offscreen OpenGL drawables.

Child windows (After Effects' composition viewer, Premiere's program monitor) render
offscreen; after each swap the drawable is copied into the toplevel window. Without
GLX_OML_sync_control (the NVIDIA driver) nothing waited for the swap: it is asynchronous
and, with the default swap interval of 1, completes at the next vblank, so the copy
always picked up the previous frame. Apps that redraw only on demand then showed stale
content until their next redraw (a paused frame stuck at draft quality, selections and
mask paths appearing a redraw late, ghosting while resizing panels).

Swap offscreen drawables without vsync (the copy is what reaches the screen) and
glFinish before the copy. Applied to the Proton-CachyOS 11.0 build as a binary patch by
lib/patch_runner.py.
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/opengl.c	2026-10-01 16:04:29.533755195 +0300
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/opengl.c	2026-10-01 16:04:29.543092306 +0300
@@ -915,6 +915,11 @@
 {
     BOOL ret = TRUE;
 
+    /* Offscreen drawables are put on screen by client_surface_present(), not by the
+     * driver. With vsync the driver completes the swap at the next vblank, after we
+     * already copied the drawable, so every copy showed the previous frame. */
+    if (gl->base.client && InterlockedCompareExchange( &gl->base.client->offscreen, 0, 0 )) interval = 0;
+
     if (interval < 0 && !has_swap_control_tear) interval = -interval;
 
     switch (swap_control_method)
@@ -1483,7 +1488,12 @@
         if (pglXWaitForSbcOML) pglXWaitForSbcOML( gdi_display, gl->drawable, target_sbc, &ust, &msc, &sbc );
     }
 
-    if (offscreen && !pglXWaitForSbcOML) XFlush( gdi_display );
+    if (offscreen && !pglXWaitForSbcOML)
+    {
+        /* no GLX_OML_sync_control (NVIDIA): make sure the swap is done before the copy */
+        funcs->p_glFinish();
+        XFlush( gdi_display );
+    }
 
     client_surface_present( base->client );
     return TRUE;
